    "body": "More from the review of PR #811 (#787, self-centering vises):\n- **The dovetail lip doesn't draw a real dovetail's inward overhang** (it lies inside the stock's box), so the decision's 'never less steel' claim overreaches slightly. The lip is also off by default: a user clamping on dovetail jaws has to enable it. Consider a hint in the dialog.\n- **No 'Centre on stock' action on a placed vise's row:** after an asymmetric stock change the user must edit the pose or re-place the vise. Add the action, as an undoable command with an MCP twin.\n- **`CENTRE_TOL` is an absolute 1e-6 mm:** a hand-typed centre to 3 decimals may be refused. Consider a relative tolerance, or snapping to the fitted centre.",
